{
 "lines": {
  "The whole machine, as far as we’ve drawn it. Every box here exists because of something to its left.": {
   "file": "7436c7df313e.m4a",
   "duration": 5480
  },
  "Inside, the box is just more boxes. Every flow that crossed the boundary still lands somewhere; nothing appears or vanishes at the edge. And look at the loop: manure feeds the fields, the fields feed the herd. Inside the boundary it’s a resource. At the gate it’s a problem.": {
   "file": "5e0f3fcc34d5.m4a",
   "duration": 16891
  },
  "Name an undesirable and it becomes a problem. A problem invites solutions, and each one is a new box with outputs of its own. The digester transforms manure into energy, and it runs on capital. What it leaves behind: leaks, and a question mark.": {
   "file": "6204ace28060.m4a",
   "duration": 16208
  },
  "The manure branch. Two answers to one problem, each leaving different things behind.": {
   "file": "dfecb72110ff.m4a",
   "duration": 4682
  },
  "Spreading on land is cheaper. But look at what it leaves: nitrate seeps into groundwater, ammonia drifts off. Both are diffuse. It doesn’t solve the problem so much as move it past the boundary.": {
   "file": "de044e94ba79.m4a",
   "duration": 12213
  },
  "Back to the digester. Neither option is clean. The question isn’t which one has no residue, but which residue you can live with, or solve next.": {
   "file": "db2e26883d84.m4a",
   "duration": 8779
  },
  "Capital goes into the digester, to build it and to keep it tight. Whether it pays is the balance across its boundary: gas revenue out, capital in. When the balance tips, the input becomes a problem. The state can answer it with a subsidy, a rule designed as a solution: the mirror image of the cap.": {
   "file": "fe7d342ac822.m4a",
   "duration": 18923
  },
  "The digester’s balance. Capital in, gas out, and a subsidy holding up one side of the scale.": {
   "file": "6bafae606fbc.m4a",
   "duration": 5628
  },
  "The water beds: a solution that turned out to be an experiment. It failed, and the farm still came out knowing more than it did.": {
   "file": "4fd7d35fbaa3.m4a",
   "duration": 7107
  },
  "The farmer had an answer for lame cows: heated water beds. Soft, warm, surely a help. But every solution is a hypothesis, and this one comes with an output nobody can name yet.": {
   "file": "6493b7821307.m4a",
   "duration": 11205
  },
  "Then the fog condensed. The herd came down with udder infections, and the vet traced them to the beds: warm and wet is exactly where bacteria thrive. The question mark gave up one secret, and kept the rest.": {
   "file": "d7f2ddc5c20e.m4a",
   "duration": 12055
  },
  "The infections became a problem, and the cheapest solution was to undo the first one. The farmer cut the beds open and took the loss. Lame cows are back on the table, but the farm now knows something it didn’t.": {
   "file": "7b991a3e27c9.m4a",
   "duration": 11572
  },
  "Every guess here has been confirmed, and joined the other outputs. The question mark stays anyway: there is always an output nobody has named yet.": {
   "file": "442804c3ab5d.m4a",
   "duration": 7721
  },
  "Some guesses are confirmed now, and sit with the other outputs. The rest are still guesses, not facts. Click one to make it a known undesirable.": {
   "file": "e60e48cc7a51.m4a",
   "duration": 8748
  },
  "Every box has an output nobody can name at design time. These are guesses, not facts, each matched to a pattern that has caught systems out before. Click one to make it a known undesirable.": {
   "file": "caccd505ae53.m4a",
   "duration": 10974
  },
  "Back to a guess. Unconfirmed, but not forgotten.": {
   "file": "31992255bf27.m4a",
   "duration": 2901
  },
  "“Efficiency gains grow the herd” is now a known undesirable, joining the farm’s outputs and becoming a problem of its own. The question mark stays, though. The fog shrinks; it never closes.": {
   "file": "285ce72fcf19.m4a",
   "duration": 11943
  },
  "“Bought feed replaces grassland” is now a known undesirable, joining the farm’s outputs and becoming a problem of its own. The question mark stays, though. The fog shrinks; it never closes.": {
   "file": "8b68fbd78b00.m4a",
   "duration": 11666
  },
  "“Routine antibiotics breed resistance” is now a known undesirable, joining the farm’s outputs and becoming a problem of its own. The question mark stays, though. The fog shrinks; it never closes.": {
   "file": "0c7d72b383d5.m4a",
   "duration": 11774
  },
  "Methane leaves the farm unpriced. Nothing inside this boundary makes it the farm’s problem. Something outside would have to: a rule, a price, a norm.": {
   "file": "5bf75b06ab50.m4a",
   "duration": 8356
  },
  "A rule arrives. It’s someone else’s solution, the state’s answer to warming, and here it lands as a problem, on purpose. A feed additive cuts methane at the source. It costs money per litre, and what it does long-term is still a question mark.": {
   "file": "9e842a4c0cc8.m4a",
   "duration": 14773
  },
  "The methane cap, and what it set in motion.": {
   "file": "2d0363c770fd.m4a",
   "duration": 2247
  },
  "Fewer cows meets the cap on paper. But the milk still gets drunk, so production moves abroad, and the methane goes with it. That’s leakage: the problem didn’t go away, it left the boundary. Draw the boundary wider and this solution could be worse than the problem.": {
   "file": "bc40202b7b59.m4a",
   "duration": 15504
  },
  "The additive again. It keeps the problem here, where it can at least be seen and measured.": {
   "file": "089b640e876d.m4a",
   "duration": 4496
  },
  "Which part? Name it, or click it, and I’ll trace what it’s there for.": {
   "file": "320a8c136ee2.m4a",
   "duration": 3793
  },
  "This prototype follows a scripted story, so I only understand a little. Try a suggestion below, or click anything on the canvas.": {
   "file": "39b883cf5a65.m4a",
   "duration": 6639
  },
  "A dairy farm, as a black box. Things go in, things come out. Some are wanted, some aren’t, and some of them we can’t name yet.": {
   "file": "2094e130c67b.m4a",
   "duration": 8183
  },
  "Follow any box back and you reach the reason it exists. Cutting the beds open answers the infections, which answer the beds, which answer lame cows, which answer the farm’s purpose: a living from milk.": {
   "file": "cb58507cabba.m4a",
   "duration": 11115
  },
  "Each part of this machine can answer one question: what are you here for? And each answer leaves something behind. That residue is the next problem.": {
   "file": "d96f02555fa3.m4a",
   "duration": 8149
  },
  "The farm turns grass, feed and care into milk. Everything else on this canvas exists because of that.": {
   "file": "6e9e9c6e0dcb.m4a",
   "duration": 6115
  },
  "Water goes in for drinking and for cleaning. It’s cheap enough that nobody counts it, which is exactly why it’s worth drawing.": {
   "file": "b5ce320c17b7.m4a",
   "duration": 5879
  },
  "Bought feed tops up what the farm’s own grass can’t provide. Every kilo carries someone else’s land with it.": {
   "file": "b706b6dea93b.m4a",
   "duration": 6864
  },
  "Genetics arrive as breeding choices. They shape the herd for a decade, long after anyone remembers making them.": {
   "file": "9403f6a32d94.m4a",
   "duration": 6550
  },
  "Energy runs the milking, the cooling and the pumps. It flows in quietly, and the farm only notices it on the bill.": {
   "file": "6130d5a66394.m4a",
   "duration": 6981
  },
  "The vet and the contractors bring skills the farm doesn’t keep in-house. They see many farms, which makes them the first to spot a pattern.": {
   "file": "70cde9998fed.m4a",
   "duration": 7141
  },
  "Milk is the reason the farm exists. Every other box on this canvas is either feeding it, or cleaning up after it.": {
   "file": "f89a29848dcf.m4a",
   "duration": 6015
  },
  "A cow has to calve to give milk, so every litre comes with a calf attached. Beef is the by-product that pays.": {
   "file": "00c87147cbe9.m4a",
   "duration": 7177
  },
  "Manure leaves the herd every day, wanted or not. On the farm’s own fields it’s fertiliser; past what the land can take, it’s a problem waiting for a name.": {
   "file": "49b5359f2a2c.m4a",
   "duration": 9340
  },
  "Methane leaves with every breath the herd takes. It used to leave for free; since the cap, every tonne counts against the farm.": {
   "file": "27b1882ffdb1.m4a",
   "duration": 8009
  },
  "Runoff is diffuse. It leaves through every field at once, a little at a time. Diffuse outputs are the hardest to solve, and the easiest to leave off the map.": {
   "file": "4261d56f8e32.m4a",
   "duration": 8748
  },
  "Feeding mixes bought feed with the farm’s own grass, so the herd eats what the land can’t fully provide.": {
   "file": "8ce38c3b1906.m4a",
   "duration": 5911
  },
  "Young stock replaces cows that leave the herd. Genetics come in here, and pay off years later.": {
   "file": "995e7d35c62f.m4a",
   "duration": 5775
  },
  "The herd is the conversion engine: feed and water in, milk, calves, manure and methane out.": {
   "file": "f45f6099c9ed.m4a",
   "duration": 6422
  },
  "Milking turns a cow’s output into a product someone will buy. It is the narrowest gate of the farm.": {
   "file": "e4ea5e4f4227.m4a",
   "duration": 6187
  },
  "Storage holds manure until the fields can take it. It’s a “contain” solution, and it’s been around so long nobody thinks of it as one.": {
   "file": "a3353fd234e8.m4a",
   "duration": 7413
  },
  "The fields close the loop: manure in, grass out. They also leak whatever they can’t hold.": {
   "file": "9f7c28f7a924.m4a",
   "duration": 5701
  },
  "Manure isn’t a problem by nature; the fields want it. It becomes one when there’s more of it than the land can absorb.": {
   "file": "6a6ef7e448ed.m4a",
   "duration": 6717
  },
  "The digester turns surplus manure into energy and a fertiliser that’s easier to handle. It costs capital to build and to keep tight.": {
   "file": "16f6fb09c3c5.m4a",
   "duration": 7138
  },
  "Spreading moves manure off the farm’s books and into the soil. What the soil can’t hold moves on, into groundwater and air.": {
   "file": "94651d1a102e.m4a",
   "duration": 7405
  },
  "Biogas is the digester’s purpose made visible: manure that was a problem leaves as energy someone will pay for.": {
   "file": "4a338c09c5bb.m4a",
   "duration": 6206
  },
  "Capital goes into the digester; it isn’t something the digester leaves behind. Every input a solution needs raises its own question: where does it come from?": {
   "file": "15e85a779687.m4a",
   "duration": 8890
  },
  "Whether the digester pays is the balance across its boundary: capital and upkeep in, gas revenue out. When the balance tips the wrong way, the input becomes a problem.": {
   "file": "fb7f0d37adda.m4a",
   "duration": 9222
  },
  "The subsidy is a rule designed as a solution: the state pays part of the bill because it wants the methane captured. It’s the mirror image of the cap.": {
   "file": "e442758e151f.m4a",
   "duration": 8253
  },
  "With the subsidy, the balance tips the right way and the digester earns its keep. On paper, the problem is solved.": {
   "file": "572a730a47d3.m4a",
   "duration": 6246
  },
  "The subsidy solves a money problem by borrowing someone else’s decision. When the policy changes, the problem comes back, and the digester is already built.": {
   "file": "96366c555388.m4a",
   "duration": 8345
  },
  "A subsidy changes behaviour beyond its target. Who else builds a digester, just because the money is there? Nobody knows yet.": {
   "file": "8134d0b37641.m4a",
   "duration": 6461
  },
  "Digestate is what’s left after digestion: the nutrients without most of the smell, easier to dose on the fields. The loop to the land stays intact.": {
   "file": "67f29e0dc0f8.m4a",
   "duration": 8276
  },
  "No digester is perfectly tight. A little methane escapes from every seal, so a solution built to capture methane releases some of its own.": {
   "file": "b506afbee62f.m4a",
   "duration": 8297
  },
  "Even a well-understood machine leaves room for surprise. The question mark stays, because no design names every output.": {
   "file": "98e62376cd92.m4a",
   "duration": 6755
  },
  "Spread at the right time and rate, manure feeds the soil. This is the loop the fields were made for.": {
   "file": "336a888fd399.m4a",
   "duration": 5935
  },
  "What the crop can’t take up washes down into the groundwater. It leaves a little at a time, from every field, and turns up years later in someone’s drinking water.": {
   "file": "f42a1e8957bf.m4a",
   "duration": 10343
  },
  "Ammonia drifts off the moment manure meets the air. It comes down again on nature that can’t take the extra nitrogen.": {
   "file": "4aac77adb4d8.m4a",
   "duration": 7124
  },
  "What decades of spreading do to the soil, nobody can fully say yet. The question mark is honest about it.": {
   "file": "b80ae0b2f33d.m4a",
   "duration": 5968
  },
  "Warming is the state’s problem, not the farm’s. Seen from here it’s background, until a rule brings it inside.": {
   "file": "9f11d66c357a.m4a",
   "duration": 6507
  },
  "The cap is someone else’s solution. For the state it answers warming; for the farm it is a new problem, created on purpose.": {
   "file": "b453a5dbb5a3.m4a",
   "duration": 7495
  },
  "Methane was always leaving the farm. The cap is what makes it this farm’s problem.": {
   "file": "cc97e107f2b6.m4a",
   "duration": 4587
  },
  "The additive suppresses methane in the rumen, at the source. It works today; what it does over a cow’s lifetime is still a question mark.": {
   "file": "baf760bbba63.m4a",
   "duration": 7721
  },
  "Fewer cows meets the cap on paper. The milk is still drunk somewhere, so production and its methane move abroad.": {
   "file": "9b3603bfb625.m4a",
   "duration": 6732
  },
  "The additive does what it promises: less methane per cow, measured at the source. The cap is met.": {
   "file": "5c2f5759748b.m4a",
   "duration": 5282
  },
  "The additive has to be bought every day, for every cow. Meeting the cap becomes a running cost on every litre.": {
   "file": "ab5b1e3908ff.m4a",
   "duration": 6225
  },
  "The additive is new. What it does to the cow, the milk or the soil over many years is still a question mark.": {
   "file": "7d6df00928c1.m4a",
   "duration": 6078
  },
  "Fewer cows, less methane. Here, at least.": {
   "file": "52a359c5b087.m4a",
   "duration": 2851
  },
  "Fewer cows means less milk, and less milk means less income. The cap is met by shrinking the very thing the farm exists for.": {
   "file": "a39823b86f13.m4a",
   "duration": 7088
  },
  "Demand for milk doesn’t shrink with the herd. A farm somewhere else fills the gap, and the methane leaves from there instead.": {
   "file": "7c7c199a88bf.m4a",
   "duration": 6573
  },
  "Shrinking a herd changes more than the numbers: the land, the work, the next generation’s choice to farm. None of it has a name yet.": {
   "file": "d312e02379b8.m4a",
   "duration": 8582
  },
  "Cows that lie badly stand too long, and their legs pay for it. Lameness costs milk and makes cows suffer.": {
   "file": "85ad486a9512.m4a",
   "duration": 7188
  },
  "The farmer chose heated water beds, believing they would help: soft and warm, so cows lie longer and their legs recover. A clear purpose, and an untested one.": {
   "file": "514cc7da59ce.m4a",
   "duration": 9572
  },
  "The beds did what they were chosen for. Cows lay longer, and their legs recovered. The intended output arrived, as intended.": {
   "file": "5fc115ab43a4.m4a",
   "duration": 7186
  },
  "Warm and wet is exactly where bacteria thrive. Nobody named this output at design time; the herd showed it, and the vet traced it back to the beds.": {
   "file": "0158b901f772.m4a",
   "duration": 8598
  },
  "Every solution is a hypothesis. The beds had a clear purpose, and outputs nobody had named yet. One of them has surfaced; the rest are still fog.": {
   "file": "87310639f693.m4a",
   "duration": 8216
  },
  "An output nobody could name became one nobody could ignore.": {
   "file": "55c096448125.m4a",
   "duration": 2765
  },
  "Sometimes the best solution to a problem is to undo the solution that caused it. The farmer cut every bed open and took the loss.": {
   "file": "e7bc12dcc80f.m4a",
   "duration": 6835
  },
  "The beds were paid for, and now they’re gone. Accepting the loss is part of the solution: the money won’t come back, but the infections stop.": {
   "file": "820c1e26fb6b.m4a",
   "duration": 8227
  },
  "The experiment failed, and the farm knows something it didn’t: warm and wet breeds bacteria. That knowledge is an output too, and it will shape the next solution.": {
   "file": "8dd980cd0ce5.m4a",
   "duration": 8754
  },
  "Undoing a solution is a solution too, with outputs of its own. Where cutting the beds open leads, nobody can say yet.": {
   "file": "7d4ffbcbcf3d.m4a",
   "duration": 7241
  },
  "If each cow gets cheaper to keep, the rational move is more cows. Total manure and methane rise even as each cow improves.": {
   "file": "f0d76d59c63a.m4a",
   "duration": 7051
  },
  "Imported feed is easier than growing grass. Over time the land, and the skill of farming it, wither, and the farm depends on a supply chain it can’t see.": {
   "file": "b4dd81dc460e.m4a",
   "duration": 8774
  },
  "Preventive treatment keeps the herd healthy this year and makes treatment weaker for everyone later.": {
   "file": "7a90d1899dcf.m4a",
   "duration": 4866
  },
  "A product team, as a black box. Requests and guidance go in, features and a running service come out. So do bugs that escape, and debt that piles up quietly, and things nobody can name yet.": {
   "file": "4afb6d9bbd42.m4a",
   "duration": 12871
  },
  "Inside, requests become cards, cards cross the board, code is built and reviewed, and the test pipeline sends what it catches back to the backlog. Inside the boundary a bug is work. Past the release it’s an incident with a customer’s name on it.": {
   "file": "9f0b5bea1f56.m4a",
   "duration": 15496
  },
  "The team exists to turn what customers need into software they can rely on. Everything on this canvas, the board, the gates, the targets, is there because of that, or because of something that was.": {
   "file": "ab84872b44d3.m4a",
   "duration": 11412
  },
  "Requests arrive from customers, sales and support, more of them than any team can build. Choosing among them is the first thing the team does.": {
   "file": "23462b1a6f1c.m4a",
   "duration": 7021
  },
  "Product management sits outside the team and guides its product owners: what matters, for whom, by when. It arrives as priorities, and sometimes as dates.": {
   "file": "5f83a858b28b.m4a",
   "duration": 9286
  },
  "The one input that can’t be bought faster. Every other choice here is about spending it.": {
   "file": "121555c2dc8c.m4a",
   "duration": 4812
  },
  "Servers, pipelines and licences. Rented by the hour, so they show up on a bill instead of a board.": {
   "file": "d4071de0ad84.m4a",
   "duration": 6248
  },
  "Most of the running code was written by strangers, for free. It ages on their schedule, not the team’s.": {
   "file": "c6acc611c580.m4a",
   "duration": 6009
  },
  "What customers asked for, shipped. It’s what the roadmap counts.": {
   "file": "ae20cbdc17e5.m4a",
   "duration": 3409
  },
  "Software only helps while it runs. Keeping it running is half the work and almost none of the roadmap.": {
   "file": "e440ad411f4d.m4a",
   "duration": 4871
  },
  "Every team ships bugs. The ones caught inside become cards; the ones that escape become a customer’s bad day.": {
   "file": "f1cb69ac1db6.m4a",
   "duration": 7208
  },
  "Every shortcut is a loan against future work. It leaves no single trace, just a team that gets a little slower every quarter.": {
   "file": "9f84901e775a.m4a",
   "duration": 7107
  },
  "Every system has outputs nobody can name at design time. The question mark is honest about it.": {
   "file": "1cfe17695286.m4a",
   "duration": 5348
  },
  "Where requests, guidance and caught bugs queue up as cards. The product owner orders it; the order is the strategy.": {
   "file": "14eeda9d60be.m4a",
   "duration": 7058
  },
  "Scrum or kanban, the board makes work visible: what’s being done, what’s stuck, what’s next.": {
   "file": "674c32e9c00a.m4a",
   "duration": 6307
  },
  "Engineers turn cards into code and check each other’s. Where the time goes, and where shortcuts get taken.": {
   "file": "2533eb537b9a.m4a",
   "duration": 6099
  },
  "Every change runs the tests. What fails goes back to the backlog: a bug caught inside is just another card.": {
   "file": "9c7a0b5cc03d.m4a",
   "duration": 6539
  },
  "The boundary that matters: before it, a bug costs the team; after it, the customer.": {
   "file": "9803efe7a63d.m4a",
   "duration": 4717
  },
  "Someone watches the service at three in the morning. Their pager is where escaped bugs come home.": {
   "file": "3ef6278b4880.m4a",
   "duration": 4967
  },
  "A bug the pipeline catches is a card. A bug a customer catches is an escalation, a hotfix and a dent in trust.": {
   "file": "2e1dd349d414.m4a",
   "duration": 8610
  },
  "Escaped bugs become a problem the day a customer finds one first. The obvious answer is a gate: QA signs off every release. Fewer bugs get out. Releases slow down, and quality quietly becomes someone else’s job.": {
   "file": "7a35c72bb2ce.m4a",
   "duration": 14024
  },
  "“Customers find bugs”. Two answers to one problem, each leaving different things behind.": {
   "file": "4e6c2db4150a.m4a",
   "duration": 4499
  },
  "A QA department tests each release before it goes out: contain the bugs at the boundary. It works, and it moves the boundary.": {
   "file": "a43531851b84.m4a",
   "duration": 7267
  },
  "A QA gate again: contain the bugs at the release, at the cost of speed and of who owns quality.": {
   "file": "94ffb22181a5.m4a",
   "duration": 5896
  },
  "The gate needs people behind it: testers outside the team, with their own queue and their own manager.": {
   "file": "dd11deffc910.m4a",
   "duration": 4900
  },
  "The gate catches what the team missed. Fewer bugs reach customers.": {
   "file": "c75642684f84.m4a",
   "duration": 3552
  },
  "Every release waits its turn in QA’s queue. Changes pile up, so each release is bigger, and riskier.": {
   "file": "d2a40a801a44.m4a",
   "duration": 6124
  },
  "With a gate behind them, developers test less. The gate works, so it’s needed more: shifting the burden.": {
   "file": "edfddb3a6ab7.m4a",
   "duration": 5664
  },
  "What a separate QA department does to the team, over years, nobody can fully say.": {
   "file": "1dad21bef050.m4a",
   "duration": 4615
  },
  "The team writes tests that run on every change: eliminate escapes at the source by catching bugs where they’re cheap.": {
   "file": "956a49c53a65.m4a",
   "duration": 6350
  },
  "Tests in the pipeline instead: catch bugs at the commit, inside the boundary, where they’re only work. The price is tests to maintain, and the ones that fail at random.": {
   "file": "ef0ce380f96c.m4a",
   "duration": 9664
  },
  "A bug caught minutes after it’s written costs minutes. The customer never meets it.": {
   "file": "4282e90e7f88.m4a",
   "duration": 4351
  },
  "Tests are code too. Every feature now comes with tests to write and keep up to date.": {
   "file": "475ec1852855.m4a",
   "duration": 5788
  },
  "Some tests fail at random. Once people learn to rerun until green, the pipeline stops meaning anything.": {
   "file": "345db1d30c10.m4a",
   "duration": 6085
  },
  "What a pipeline teaches a team to ignore, nobody knows yet.": {
   "file": "e5d8951cf1bd.m4a",
   "duration": 3308
  },
  "A competitor shipped first. That’s product management’s problem, not the team’s, until a date brings it inside.": {
   "file": "43ce498f8959.m4a",
   "duration": 6331
  },
  "The date is someone else’s solution. For product management it answers a competitor; for the team it is a new problem, made on purpose.": {
   "file": "520f07b384c2.m4a",
   "duration": 7252
  },
  "Features were always slow to come. The date is what makes too few of them a problem by Q3.": {
   "file": "39e78c122f11.m4a",
   "duration": 5512
  },
  "A date arrives. It’s product management’s answer to a competitor, and here it lands as a problem, on purpose: the scope won’t fit. Cutting scope meets the date with less, and breaks promises somebody already made upstream.": {
   "file": "b43f37b13c68.m4a",
   "duration": 13500
  },
  "“Too much for Q3”. Two answers to one problem, each leaving different things behind.": {
   "file": "b02c12f97701.m4a",
   "duration": 4660
  },
  "The product owner keeps the date and drops what won’t fit. Honest, and someone upstream has to hear it.": {
   "file": "b988ecbac537.m4a",
   "duration": 5724
  },
  "Cut the scope instead. What it leaves behind: promises broken upstream and a question mark.": {
   "file": "27bbb1959b93.m4a",
   "duration": 5220
  },
  "Q3 is met, with less in it. What shipped works.": {
   "file": "4a88ef42851c.m4a",
   "duration": 3409
  },
  "Product management sold the full scope already. The cut lands on their credibility, with customers and with sales.": {
   "file": "fb72246a761a.m4a",
   "duration": 6128
  },
  "What dropped scope does to next quarter’s roadmap, nobody can say yet.": {
   "file": "c1d30b5cb17f.m4a",
   "duration": 3820
  },
  "The team keeps the scope and the date by not testing. The problem doesn’t go away; it moves somewhere slower.": {
   "file": "04931c294bda.m4a",
   "duration": 6335
  },
  "Or keep the full scope and skip the tests. The date is met in full, and the cost moves: into debt, and into the bugs customers will find. That’s the first branch again, fed from here.": {
   "file": "4a894f8868fe.m4a",
   "duration": 10701
  },
  "Everything promised, by Q3. On the roadmap, it looks like a win.": {
   "file": "e6a1e5153e45.m4a",
   "duration": 3614
  },
  "Untested code is code nobody dares to change. Next quarter starts slower.": {
   "file": "27db87f5c0c1.m4a",
   "duration": 5104
  },
  "What wasn’t tested gets tested by customers. It feeds straight back into the first problem: customers find the bugs.": {
   "file": "a942a7d7e778.m4a",
   "duration": 5924
  },
  "A team that learns the date beats the tests learns something else too. Nobody can say yet what.": {
   "file": "f2219c5d1a2d.m4a",
   "duration": 5317
  },
  "Without a forecast, product management can’t promise and sales can’t sell. Predictability is what the people outside the box ask for.": {
   "file": "24a5d65d23ab.m4a",
   "duration": 7882
  },
  "Inside the team, a problem: nobody can say when anything will be done. Management sets velocity targets, believing that what gets measured gets delivered. The burn-up charts steady. What else the targets do is still a question mark.": {
   "file": "1ea0db029569.m4a",
   "duration": 13544
  },
  "“Velocity targets”: a solution that turned out to be an experiment. It failed, and the team still came out knowing more than it did.": {
   "file": "38b090cfb68c.m4a",
   "duration": 7142
  },
  "Management chose velocity targets, believing a number to aim for would make delivery steady. A clear purpose, and an untested one.": {
   "file": "a4b1c4028a2c.m4a",
   "duration": 6613
  },
  "The targets did what they were chosen for. The charts went up and to the right, sprint after sprint.": {
   "file": "0e7d339741b3.m4a",
   "duration": 5315
  },
  "A three-point story became a five. Nobody cheated; everyone estimated a little safer. Nobody named this output at design time; product management traced it, comparing charts with what shipped.": {
   "file": "3e5f8ec837dd.m4a",
   "duration": 11743
  },
  "Then the fog condensed: story-point inflation. Velocity rose every sprint and features didn’t. Product management noticed first, comparing the charts with what actually shipped.": {
   "file": "a140c598b819.m4a",
   "duration": 10348
  },
  "Every solution is a hypothesis. The targets had a clear purpose, and outputs nobody had named yet.": {
   "file": "8e2e82652bfa.m4a",
   "duration": 5575
  },
  "Once points inflate, the forecast they were meant to give is worse than having none.": {
   "file": "9a08de225f72.m4a",
   "duration": 3942
  },
  "An output nobody could name became one nobody could ignore. Points mean nothing now, so management drops the targets. The dashboards go dark, and the organisation knows something it didn’t.": {
   "file": "d04a4572da19.m4a",
   "duration": 10205
  },
  "“Points mean nothing”, and what its answer left behind.": {
   "file": "3623483783dd.m4a",
   "duration": 3146
  },
  "Sometimes the best solution to a problem is to undo the solution that caused it. Management dropped the targets and kept counting what shipped.": {
   "file": "bea3d5a95a09.m4a",
   "duration": 7268
  },
  "The charts everybody watched are gone. For a while, nobody outside the team knows how it’s doing.": {
   "file": "90d2e32d69ce.m4a",
   "duration": 5637
  },
  "When a measure becomes a target, it stops measuring. The experiment failed, and that knowledge is an output too.": {
   "file": "9e590f976abb.m4a",
   "duration": 5939
  },
  "Undoing a solution is a solution too, with outputs of its own.": {
   "file": "5ee8cc40461c.m4a",
   "duration": 3713
  },
  "Upgrades never beat features for a sprint slot. Each skipped one makes the next bigger, until “legacy” is the accepted state.": {
   "file": "9d00a104c221.m4a",
   "duration": 7055
  },
  "“Libraries age into obsolescence” is now a known undesirable, joining the team’s outputs and becoming a problem of its own. The question mark stays, though. The fog shrinks; it never closes.": {
   "file": "bed69b2a101c.m4a",
   "duration": 12532
  },
  "An urgent fix skips the tests to reach customers faster, and ships the next bug with it.": {
   "file": "d212df3a9d1c.m4a",
   "duration": 4985
  },
  "“Hotfixes bypass the pipeline” is now a known undesirable, joining the team’s outputs and becoming a problem of its own. The question mark stays, though. The fog shrinks; it never closes.": {
   "file": "620cb16b3350.m4a",
   "duration": 10776
  },
  "Dates squeeze the team, shortcuts slip the dates, and each side’s fix makes the other’s problem worse.": {
   "file": "1389eebf6e7a.m4a",
   "duration": 5667
  },
  "“Product and teams blame each other” is now a known undesirable, joining the team’s outputs and becoming a problem of its own. The question mark stays, though. The fog shrinks; it never closes.": {
   "file": "c3c9d07f06e5.m4a",
   "duration": 11322
  },
  "Follow any box back and you reach the reason it exists. “Drop the targets” answers “points mean nothing”, which came from “velocity targets”, chosen to answer “delivery unpredictable”: a problem only because the team exists to deliver software customers rely on.": {
   "file": "808ea218c26d.m4a",
   "duration": 14044
  },
  "?: output of dairy farm.": {
   "file": "e1a4b75c9133.m4a",
   "duration": 1502
  },
  "“Infected udders”, and what its answer left behind.": {
   "file": "d318443447d4.m4a",
   "duration": 2853
  },
  "Someone walks into a hardware store. They want a drill. Or do they?": {
   "file": "1820c11d9d94.m4a",
   "duration": 3514
  },
  "Nobody wants a drill. They want a hole in the wall. The drill is just how you get one.": {
   "file": "a9adb2917f3f.m4a",
   "duration": 4986
  },
  "Nobody wants a hole either. It’s there for a plug and a screw: something to hang a thing on.": {
   "file": "84c214fb03d1.m4a",
   "duration": 4474
  },
  "And the screw is there to hold a picture. That’s what they came in for: a picture on the wall. Everything below it is means.": {
   "file": "07d5522a736b.m4a",
   "duration": 8722
  },
  "Why a picture? To make a room feel like theirs. The ladder keeps going, as far as you care to climb.": {
   "file": "2ea7dd502aa3.m4a",
   "duration": 5145
  },
  "The whole ladder: feeling at home, a picture, a screw, a hole, a drill. Each rung answers the one above it.": {
   "file": "97184053eb0b.m4a",
   "duration": 8090
  },
  "What does this way leave behind? The drill: dust and noise, and a gamble with what’s behind the plaster. The hole: it stays when you move out. The plug and screw: they hold anything. That’s the strength of this way.": {
   "file": "371676da4451.m4a",
   "duration": 14053
  },
  "Up at the picture, other answers fit. Adhesive nails stick straight to the wall. They don’t need a hole, a plug or a screw, and so they don’t need a drill.": {
   "file": "3b81f256e452.m4a",
   "duration": 9044
  },
  "Three rungs skipped, and what they left behind goes with them: the dust, the gamble, the holes. The strength goes too: glue won’t hold just anything. The nails leave their own: a clean wall, a weight limit, and a question mark. Will it still hold in three years? The higher you attach a solution, the more of the ladder it lets go of, good and bad.": {
   "file": "f34834e9d8e5.m4a",
   "duration": 19843
  },
  "Back to the drill. The plug and screw hold anything, and the way there costs a hole, some dust, and a gamble with the plaster. Neither answer is clean; they leave different things behind.": {
   "file": "eca0bc7944f7.m4a",
   "duration": 10397
  },
  "Climb once more, and the picture is just one answer too. Plants would do, or a colour on the wall. The higher you climb, the more answers fit, and the less any of them looks like a drill.": {
   "file": "717cb60cfcf0.m4a",
   "duration": 10395
  },
  "The whole ladder, as far as we’ve climbed it.": {
   "file": "8368fd797229.m4a",
   "duration": 2547
  },
  "People don’t want a drill. Ask what each thing is for, climb until the answers start to multiply, and solve it there.": {
   "file": "1c037204c457.m4a",
   "duration": 6613
  },
  "The drill is what people walk into the shop for. It’s a solution, and like every solution it exists for something else.": {
   "file": "e425a09787cc.m4a",
   "duration": 6780
  },
  "Nobody wants a hole in the wall. It’s a step on the way to something, and it stays behind long after the reason for it has gone.": {
   "file": "2b9dc16d14aa.m4a",
   "duration": 7023
  },
  "The plug and screw give the picture something to hang on. They’re means too, chosen because of the drill as much as for the picture.": {
   "file": "68087dc9db2a.m4a",
   "duration": 6797
  },
  "This is what they actually want: a picture on the wall. Everything below it is one way of getting there.": {
   "file": "3b1a66ad77c7.m4a",
   "duration": 4905
  },
  "The picture is there to make a room feel like theirs. You could keep climbing, but somewhere you stop: high enough that other answers fit, low enough to act on.": {
   "file": "cd25c03c9103.m4a",
   "duration": 9550
  },
  "Drilling means dust on the floor and noise for the neighbours. Small, but nobody asked for it.": {
   "file": "92e5dede1d64.m4a",
   "duration": 4837
  },
  "The picture comes down one day; the hole doesn’t. It gets filled, sanded and painted over, often by someone else.": {
   "file": "eec5c927f0ec.m4a",
   "duration": 7373
  },
  "A pipe, a cable, a hollow wall that won’t hold a plug. Nobody knows until the bit goes in.": {
   "file": "be800b00da79.m4a",
   "duration": 5478
  },
  "A screw in a plug holds a mirror, a shelf, a heavy frame. That’s the strength of this way, and it comes from the plug and screw, not the drill.": {
   "file": "f3d16d2111f2.m4a",
   "duration": 9158
  },
  "Adhesive nails stick straight to the wall. They answer the picture, not the hole, so the hole, the plug and the screw are no longer needed, and neither is the drill.": {
   "file": "d33875b428cd.m4a",
   "duration": 8360
  },
  "Peel the nail off and the wall is as it was. Nothing to fill, nothing to paint.": {
   "file": "0df8a4349926.m4a",
   "duration": 4806
  },
  "Glue holds a frame, not a mirror. Attaching higher costs something too: it only fits the needs it was made for.": {
   "file": "dc837c29a4cc.m4a",
   "duration": 5831
  },
  "Heat, damp, old paint. Whether the glue still holds in three years is a question mark, and the picture finds out first.": {
   "file": "b642b65d15a9.m4a",
   "duration": 7057
  },
  "Plants make a room feel lived in too. Up here, a picture is just one answer among many.": {
   "file": "9dd812893de2.m4a",
   "duration": 5515
  },
  "A colour on the wall does it without hanging anything at all. The higher the rung, the less the answers look like a drill.": {
   "file": "acf1e6c5b6d5.m4a",
   "duration": 6090
  },
  "A team asks for a CRM licence. Everyone buys one; it’s just what you do.": {
   "file": "e8d65f5f168b.m4a",
   "duration": 4999
  },
  "What’s the CRM for? Keeping track of customers, the way this team sells.": {
   "file": "5b8629e1aac1.m4a",
   "duration": 4171
  },
  "And that’s there for customers who come back. That’s what they actually want. The licence is one way of getting there.": {
   "file": "58251a8773ed.m4a",
   "duration": 6014
  },
  "The ladder as far as it matters here: customers who come back, kept track of the way this team sells. The licence answers that from below.": {
   "file": "ead34b4d3d8d.m4a",
   "duration": 7854
  },
  "What does the package leave behind? It works on day one, and someone else keeps it running. It also costs a licence per seat, every year. And it was made for everyone, so it fits no one exactly: workarounds, and spreadsheets on the side. Plus a question mark: the vendor’s roadmap.": {
   "file": "bfc7c917b936.m4a",
   "duration": 13900
  },
  "Why not build our own? Because of a rule: crafting software is expensive. It takes a team, months, and several tries to get right. Under that rule, buying generic is the sensible answer. The package is there because of the rule, not because it fits.": {
   "file": "33add3dbf686.m4a",
   "duration": 15106
  },
  "Under the rule, building your own means a team and months of work before anything runs. That’s why the package won. Ask what has changed.": {
   "file": "68c7e2b4cb1e.m4a",
   "duration": 7628
  },
  "Agentic AI changes the rule. Crafting gets cheap: a working version in days, changed as often as the work changes. The rule that made buying sensible is weakening, and the answer it kept off the table is back on it.": {
   "file": "c5a2fd11811a.m4a",
   "duration": 13064
  },
  "Built to fit. It follows the way this team sells, and there’s no licence. The workarounds go, and so does the vendor’s roadmap. It leaves its own: the upkeep is ours now, and a question mark. Who understands it in three years? Neither answer is clean. But the rule that decided between them has changed.": {
   "file": "d964e4a9f871.m4a",
   "duration": 19157
  },
  "Back to the package. It works on day one and someone else runs it, and it costs a licence, a roadmap that isn’t ours, and a way of working bent to fit.": {
   "file": "e2573162a2f4.m4a",
   "duration": 9204
  },
  "The whole picture, as far as we’ve looked.": {
   "file": "1571e87d24c8.m4a",
   "duration": 2049
  },
  "Generic software was a sound answer to a rule: crafting is expensive. When a rule changes, go back to the answers it shaped.": {
   "file": "3a46db622233.m4a",
   "duration": 7549
  },
  "A CRM package is what teams ask for. It’s a solution, made for every team at once, and it exists for something else.": {
   "file": "cb6d2a07b2d3.m4a",
   "duration": 7280
  },
  "Keeping track of customers, the way this team actually sells. The package knows customers; it doesn’t know this team.": {
   "file": "eca706d19389.m4a",
   "duration": 6946
  },
  "This is what they want: customers who come back. Everything below it is one way of getting there.": {
   "file": "edbd873bd984.m4a",
   "duration": 5595
  },
  "Install it, add users, go. Someone else wrote it, tested it and keeps it running. That’s the real strength of buying.": {
   "file": "eef43bfdb91e.m4a",
   "duration": 6527
  },
  "The bill comes every year, for every seat, whether the team uses half the features or all of them.": {
   "file": "10e4056e1ef9.m4a",
   "duration": 5764
  },
  "Built for everyone, it fits no one exactly. The team bends its way of selling to the tool, and what doesn’t fit ends up in a spreadsheet.": {
   "file": "cd215c1b27f5.m4a",
   "duration": 8264
  },
  "Prices change, features go, the vendor gets bought. The roadmap is someone else’s, and so is the question mark.": {
   "file": "645e0c4d730e.m4a",
   "duration": 6343
  },
  "Software takes a team, months, and several tries to get right. Under that rule, buying something generic is the sensible answer.": {
   "file": "530c5192c567.m4a",
   "duration": 7676
  },
  "Software made for this team: its customers, its way of selling. Under the old rule, too slow and too dear. Under the new one, a real answer.": {
   "file": "d3514d22875c.m4a",
   "duration": 8906
  },
  "It follows the way the team sells, and it changes when the team does. No workarounds, no spreadsheet on the side.": {
   "file": "cf5b57c4fd70.m4a",
   "duration": 6835
  },
  "Nothing to pay per seat. The cost moves from a licence to the work of keeping it right.": {
   "file": "426648861f53.m4a",
   "duration": 3858
  },
  "Nobody else patches it, hosts it or answers when it breaks. Cheaper to make is not the same as free to keep.": {
   "file": "8ba27c7ad4e6.m4a",
   "duration": 6540
  },
  "Code an agent wrote in a week still has to make sense to someone in three years. Whether it does is the new question mark.": {
   "file": "a4ab3576765a.m4a",
   "duration": 6412
  }
 }
}
